-- both clauses of the admission test are needed, and this is the proof. Cyclohexane's count changes with
-- the temperature at a fixed medium: drop the rate clause and that difference disappears. Glycerol's
-- changes with the medium at a fixed temperature: drop the handedness clause and that one disappears.
-- Neither clause is a special case of the other, and the test with two clauses is the smallest one that
-- gets both compounds right. The pair is also the answer to the obvious objection -- that the right fix
-- is to record the stereochemistry and be done -- since no amount of stereochemistry in the record
-- determines cyclohexane's count, and no amount of kinetics determines glycerol's.
both-clauses-needed : (a : signals-at 18 cyh-motions cyh-h 30 nmr-achiral ≡ signals-at 18 cyh-motions cyh-h 19 nmr-achiral → Empty) × (signals-at 14 glc-temp-motions num-glc-obs 30 any-rate-achiral ≡ signals-at 14 glc-temp-motions num-glc-obs 30 any-rate-chiral → Empty)
both-clauses-needed = (cyh-temperature-decides , glc-medium-decides)
